module mn-state-rules

/// `lit/mn-rules` is a base library: it declares what Minnesota's court
/// packages share and no procedure of its own. Its pack holds only this
/// placeholder terminal, which no link or case may route through.
start library

terminal library: "Minnesota state court rules library (no procedure)"

/// A principal brief: at most 45 pages, exclusive of the tables and any
/// addendum, or 14,000 words, or 1,300 lines of monospaced text, except for
/// good cause and with the court's permission; a word or line count is
/// certified (Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01, subd. 3(a)). A motion to file
/// an enlarged brief is filed at least 14 days before the brief is due.
limit principal-brief {
  words <= 14_000 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
  lines <= 1_300 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
  pages <= 45 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
} cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"

/// A reply brief: at most 20 pages, or 7,000 words, or 650 lines of
/// monospaced text (Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01, subd. 3(b)).
limit reply-brief {
  words <= 7_000 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
  lines <= 650 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
  pages <= 20 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"
} cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 132.01"

/// A petition for review, and a response to it: at most 2,000 words,
/// exclusive of the caption, signature block and addendum, with a
/// Certificate of Document Length (Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 117, subds. 3, 4).
limit review-petition {
  words <= 2_000 cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 117"
} cite "Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 117"

/// The appellant serves and files its brief and addendum (Minn. R. Civ.
/// App. P. 131.01, subd. 1).
event AppellantBriefFiled() paper principal-brief
/// The respondent serves and files its brief (Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 131.01,
/// subd. 2).
event RespondentBriefFiled() paper principal-brief
/// The appellant serves and files a reply brief (Minn. R. Civ. App. P.
/// 131.01, subd. 3).
event ReplyBriefFiled() paper reply-brief
// The trigger events the court packages' graphs route on.
/// An action, claim, petition or charge is filed and the proceeding begins.
event ActionCommenced()
/// A final judgment, decision or appealable order is entered.
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A notice of appeal, or a petition or appeal for review of a lower court's or tribunal's decision, is filed.
event NoticeOfAppealFiled()
/// The record on appeal or review is filed or transmitted.
event RecordFiled()
/// The reviewing court's or tribunal's decision or opinion is filed.
event DecisionFiled()
/// A petition for discretionary review in a higher court (certiorari, transfer, leave or review) is filed:
/// in Minnesota, the petition for review of a Court of Appeals decision (Minn. R. Civ. App. P. 117, subd. 1).
event ReviewPetitionFiled() paper review-petition
/// The mandate, remittitur or certificate of judgment issues.
event MandateIssued()
